    <GaugingStation location="Invergairn" name="Gairn" number="12006">
        <Comments>
            <Comment type="Station Summary">Velocity area station gauging catchment with natural regime, although flows can be affected by frozen catchment.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Hydrometric">Natural control includes rubble from early gabion construction (broken up by spate of Nov 1978). Frozen catchment can produce notable low flows (e.g. 22/01/1985). Two peak flow ratings applied to entire record, derived from current meter gaugings. Peak flow rating 1 gaugings up to 1.3m (0.6QMED); peak flow rating 2 gaugings up to 1.4m (about 0.8 QMED); simple extrapolation beyond.</Comment>
            <Comment type="General">Velocity area station with cableway; about 15m wide section.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow regime">Natural regime.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Catchment">Upland catchment with mountainous headwaters often snowy in winter. Some Dalradian metamorphics, mainly granite intrusive. Half of catchment overlain by superficial deposits. Landuse pastoral and mountain moorland; some forestry. No significant catchment changes known. Catchment rainfall may be underestimated.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Factors affecting runoff">N</Comment>
        </Comments>
        <Usages>
            <Usage notes="No comment." suitable="Yes" type="QMED"/>
            <Usage notes="No comment." suitable="Yes" type="Pooling"/>
        </Usages>
    </GaugingStation>
